# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# The app is plain files with no build step, so nothing is content-hashed and a
# filename can never prove it is current. Caching hard would therefore risk the
# exact failure this replaced: new HTML paired with old JavaScript.
#
# So everything revalidates. That is far cheaper than it sounds — the browser
# sends its ETag, Cloudflare answers 304 Not Modified in a couple of hundred
# bytes, and only genuinely changed files transfer. In return a deploy is live
# the moment it finishes, with no cache window at all.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

# A share link carries one person's slot in the fragment, which never leaves the
# browser. Belt and braces: keep referrers off these too.
/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
